{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"e275423333af576a","name":"card_unit_10th_para_battalion","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/CovertOp/units/card_unit_10th_para_battalion","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"10th PARA BATTALION","text":"Deployment: Gets +1+1 and Blitz if you have given an order this turn.","flavorText":"The 10th Battalion was an airborne infantry battalion of the Parachute Regiment of the British Army during WWII. The battalion was originally raised around volunteers from the Royal Sussex Regiment in Egypt and assigned to the 4th Parachute Brigade. The battalion saw its first action in Operation Slapstick, which was part of the Allied invasion of Italy in 1943. It was then held as reserve during the Normandy landings, but saw action again during Operation Market Garden in September 1944. On the second day of the Battle of Arnhem, they landed but failed to reach their designated target. Over the course of two days of intense combat, the battalion was gradually destroyed. Those who survived retreated to the divisional position at Oosterbeek, and after bravely holding their ground within the perimeter, the remaining few were evacuated south of the River Rhine. Unfortunately, the battalion never fully recovered from the significant losses suffered during the battle and was disbanded. The surviving soldiers were reassigned to various battalions within the 1st Parachute Brigade.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":1},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_10th_para_battalion","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_10th_para_battalion_title","SourceString":"10th PARA BATTALION","LocalizedString":"10th PARA BATTALION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":1,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_10th_para_battalion_text","SourceString":"Deployment: 